Hey, Sorn! Sorn! Sorn!

270
00:19:30,160 --> 00:19:32,240
-Boat! Boat, you’re a doctor! Help!
-Call the police! I mean, call the ambulance!

271
00:19:32,480 --> 00:19:34,680
Boat, he’s dying! Come help him!

272
00:19:35,760 --> 00:19:37,560
Don’t just stand there! Come and help!

273
00:19:38,120 --> 00:19:39,720
Sorn! Sorn!

274
00:19:39,720 --> 00:19:42,000
-What’s wrong with you?
-Boat, help him!

275
00:19:42,560 --> 00:19:44,160
Help! Somebody, help!!

276
00:19:44,640 --> 00:19:46,800
Somebody, help!!

277
00:19:52,640 --> 00:19:54,400
(Hey, stop it.)

278
00:20:05,760 --> 00:20:06,360
Pa!!

279
00:20:13,640 --> 00:20:15,600
How long have you been lying to me, Sun?

280
00:20:18,280 --> 00:20:19,400
Pa, I can explain

281
00:20:30,240 --> 00:20:30,960
Boat,

282
00:20:32,240 --> 00:20:34,320
why didn’t you wear a facemask when you
went out?

283
00:20:34,920 --> 00:20:36,080
They all know about me.

284
00:20:39,160 --> 00:20:40,000
Come inside.

285
00:20:40,600 --> 00:20:41,520
Come talk inside!

286
00:20:42,720 --> 00:20:43,600
We don’t need to talk!

287
00:20:44,240 --> 00:20:45,920
Maybe they already knew about me.

288
00:20:49,560 --> 00:20:50,280
Why, Dad?

289
00:20:52,160 --> 00:20:53,280
Are you embarrassed

290
00:20:54,280 --> 00:20:55,280
to have me as a son?

291
00:20:58,720 --> 00:21:00,560
Why can’t you just be like your brother, huh?

292
00:21:01,080 --> 00:21:02,920
He’s not studying medicine
but he’s brought home

293
00:21:02,920 --> 00:21:04,680
so many rewards, unlike you.

294
00:21:11,080 --> 00:21:11,880
Fine, Dad.

295
00:21:15,520 --> 00:21:16,760
From now on,

296
00:21:20,720 --> 00:21:22,400
I’m not one of your sons anymore.

297
00:21:23,680 --> 00:21:24,440
What the hell?

298
00:21:25,240 --> 00:21:25,920
Boat!

299
00:21:27,400 --> 00:21:27,880
Boat!!

300
00:21:40,880 --> 00:21:42,040
I don’t know

301
00:21:44,160 --> 00:21:47,080
how things will turn out if we talk to my dad directly.

302
00:21:55,120 --> 00:21:56,480
We’ll get through this.

303
00:21:58,680 --> 00:21:59,600
I will never leave you.

304
00:22:01,400 --> 00:22:02,600
‘Cause you’re my boyfriend.

305
00:22:54,560 --> 00:22:55,280
Now...

306
00:22:57,440 --> 00:22:59,880
What are you gonna do?

307
00:23:03,800 --> 00:23:04,800
I have no idea.

308
00:23:09,640 --> 00:23:10,720
I just don’t wanna go home.

309
00:23:15,680 --> 00:23:16,560
Maybe…

310
00:23:18,240 --> 00:23:19,920
I will stay with my mom at my grandma’s house.

311
00:23:21,000 --> 00:23:22,800
My mom’s there taking care of her.

312
00:23:27,800 --> 00:23:29,240
Then…I’ll figure something out.

313
00:23:38,760 --> 00:23:39,960
If you need anything at all,

314
00:23:40,120 --> 00:23:41,440
let me know, okay?

315
00:23:44,200 --> 00:23:45,880
You can lean on me, always.

316
00:23:46,960 --> 00:23:49,600
Please remember I’m here for you.

317
00:24:37,200 --> 00:24:37,680
Pa…

318
00:24:52,280 --> 00:24:52,880
I...

319
00:24:58,920 --> 00:25:01,000
Bay and I… We’ve been seeing each other
for a while.

320
00:25:07,200 --> 00:25:08,240
I’m sorry, Pa.

321
00:25:18,040 --> 00:25:18,520
Sun…

322
00:25:22,400 --> 00:25:23,800
I’m begging you.

323
00:25:33,080 --> 00:25:36,800
You know what that family has done to us.

324
00:25:38,760 --> 00:25:41,960
They’re the reason your mom and your brother moved out.

325
00:25:44,080 --> 00:25:46,040
Now you’re gonna leave me too?

326
00:26:01,120 --> 00:26:01,600
Dad…

327
00:26:04,960 --> 00:26:07,080
I have something to confess.

328
00:26:07,080 --> 00:26:09,720
Confess? What is it?

329
00:26:11,440 --> 00:26:14,000
Well, now Sun and I,

330
00:26:19,240 --> 00:26:20,400
we are boyfriends, Dad.

331
00:26:23,400 --> 00:26:24,760
You mean Chun’s son?!

332
00:26:25,760 --> 00:26:28,720
Are you insane?
How could you date someone like that?

333
00:26:30,160 --> 00:26:33,120
Why, Dad? Sun doesn’t have anything
to do with your feud.

334
00:26:33,240 --> 00:26:35,280
Of course, he does! You are my son.

335
00:26:35,400 --> 00:26:37,200
How could you ever date Chun’s son?

336
00:26:37,720 --> 00:26:39,720
How would that make me look, huh?!

337
00:26:43,920 --> 00:26:46,280
All you care about is how people see you?

338
00:26:46,360 --> 00:26:47,040
Watch it.

339
00:26:47,640 --> 00:26:48,760
I am your dad.

340
00:26:48,760 --> 00:26:49,760
You don’t get to talk back to me.

341
00:26:49,880 --> 00:26:52,160
Just listen and do as I tell you to do.

342
00:26:52,720 --> 00:26:57,000
-Dad, why can’t you listen to me?
-I’ve been working my ass off raising two sons.

343
00:26:57,800 --> 00:27:00,640
How can both of you be so ungrateful, huh?!

344
00:27:00,800 --> 00:27:02,240
But how is this my fault, Dad?

345
00:27:02,240 --> 00:27:04,320
Fine, it’s not your fault!

346
00:27:04,760 --> 00:27:07,560
But without me, could you have had
all of this, Bay?!

347
00:27:08,280 --> 00:27:11,320
Do you know what I had to do to raise you
so you could grow up

348
00:27:11,320 --> 00:27:13,440
with more opportunities than other people

349
00:27:13,440 --> 00:27:14,880
and never have to owe anyone anything?!

350
00:27:15,280 --> 00:27:18,120
But I’ve never done anything in my life to disappoint you.

351
00:27:19,520 --> 00:27:21,640
-Can’t you just let me be with Sun?
-I can’t!

352
00:27:23,200 --> 00:27:24,920
And if you don’t listen to me,

353
00:27:26,680 --> 00:27:28,240
you are not my son.

354
00:27:28,800 --> 00:27:31,000
Just get out of here. Get out of my sight!!

355
00:27:35,960 --> 00:27:37,160
These damn kids.

356
00:28:13,720 --> 00:28:14,200
Sun!

357
00:28:16,640 --> 00:28:17,200
Sun!

358
00:28:20,280 --> 00:28:20,760
Sun!

359
00:28:44,920 --> 00:28:45,920
Why, Sun?!

360
00:28:46,600 --> 00:28:48,600
Are you really giving up this easy?

361
00:28:53,920 --> 00:28:55,040
Even though you’ve given up,

362
00:28:59,520 --> 00:29:00,520
I’ll keep fighting

363
00:29:26,440 --> 00:29:29,440
CALLING BOAT

364
00:29:36,520 --> 00:29:40,920
INCOMING CALL - BAY

365
00:29:53,000 --> 00:29:53,560
Bay.

366
00:29:54,960 --> 00:29:55,960
What’s going on with you?

367
00:29:57,320 --> 00:29:58,960
You came to my house just to sit there?

368
00:30:00,560 --> 00:30:02,240
You’ve been quiet for like an hour.

369
00:30:06,960 --> 00:30:08,680
You should tell your big brother at least.

370
00:30:13,360 --> 00:30:15,320
BOAT (3)

371
00:30:15,440 --> 00:30:16,360
Who’s been calling?

372
00:30:18,360 --> 00:30:19,360
No one, Mom.

373
00:30:19,680 --> 00:30:20,880
Just some scammer.

374
00:30:22,600 --> 00:30:25,200
Did you come here because there’s something
going on at home?

375
00:30:26,480 --> 00:30:27,440
No, Mom.

376
00:30:28,320 --> 00:30:29,760
I just wanted to see Grandma.

377
00:30:32,040 --> 00:30:32,960
Hmm.

378
00:30:35,480 --> 00:30:37,960
I’m getting tired. I’ll go take a shower.

379
00:30:38,160 --> 00:30:39,520
Be with Grandma, okay?

380
00:31:10,120 --> 00:31:11,000
Sun’s mom!

381
00:31:12,000 --> 00:31:12,880
Sun’s mom!

382
00:31:13,440 --> 00:31:15,160
-Keep it down, boy!
-Sun’s mom!

383
00:31:16,520 --> 00:31:18,240
You can’t be yelling here, boy.

384
00:31:18,880 --> 00:31:19,520
Why not?

385
00:31:19,520 --> 00:31:21,280
-Come with me.
-Hey, what are you doing?

386
00:31:21,280 --> 00:31:22,360
-Come on.
-I’m not going with you?

387
00:31:22,360 --> 00:31:23,080
Bay, is that you?

388
00:31:24,720 --> 00:31:25,680
Sun’s mom, hello.

389
00:31:47,200 --> 00:31:48,240
I’ll get to the training, Dad.

390
00:31:49,080 --> 00:31:50,160
I’ll pick you up in the evening.

391
00:31:56,920 --> 00:31:57,360
Okay.

392
00:32:16,800 --> 00:32:17,160
Sun!

393
00:32:25,800 --> 00:32:26,720
Your dad has left.

394
00:32:31,840 --> 00:32:32,880
I understand

395
00:32:33,640 --> 00:32:34,760
that your dad has to come first.

396
00:32:36,760 --> 00:32:37,560
I’m not mad.

397
00:32:42,000 --> 00:32:43,640
But I’m not giving up on us that easily.

398
00:32:47,680 --> 00:32:48,440
In my eyes,

399
00:32:51,280 --> 00:32:52,560
you’re still my boyfriend

400
00:32:59,440 --> 00:33:02,760
And I know you don’t want us to break up, either.

401
00:33:07,760 --> 00:33:08,880
But I can’t choose you.

402
00:33:20,440 --> 00:33:22,000
What about our promise, Sun?

403
00:33:23,680 --> 00:33:24,440
You and me.

404
00:33:25,400 --> 00:33:28,040
An artist and a national athlete.

405
00:33:36,720 --> 00:33:37,880
You go be an artist.

406
00:33:41,400 --> 00:33:42,920
And I’ll be a national athlete.

407
00:33:50,240 --> 00:33:51,560
But we won’t be boyfriends.

408
00:34:21,400 --> 00:34:23,760
Can’t you read the sign?
‘FAMILY MEMBERS ONLY’

409
00:34:26,760 --> 00:34:27,920
You have never changed.

410
00:34:34,920 --> 00:34:35,680
What are you doing here?

411
00:34:37,680 --> 00:34:38,760
Bay came to see me.

412
00:34:43,920 --> 00:34:46,440
You don’t have the rights to dictate
what those boys do.

413
00:34:47,640 --> 00:34:49,480
Our marriage was ruined because of you.

414
00:34:53,120 --> 00:34:55,360
-It was because of Bee.
-Chun.

415
00:34:57,720 --> 00:35:00,960
Whether Bee stole your family’s recipe or not,

416
00:35:02,640 --> 00:35:05,600
you don’t have to hold a grudge
for the rest of your life.

417
00:35:06,480 --> 00:35:12,280
And there’s no need to drag me and your children
into your feud.

418
00:35:13,000 --> 00:35:13,920
-It’s him...
-Chun

419
00:35:14,080 --> 00:35:15,920
I didn’t leave you because of someone else.

420
00:35:16,480 --> 00:35:19,040
It’s because you still can’t let this go.

421
00:35:22,720 --> 00:35:25,360
I should’ve taken Sun with me too.

422
00:35:26,160 --> 00:35:27,640
Then you could’ve fought with Bee

423
00:35:27,800 --> 00:35:29,680
without causing Sun all this pain.

424
00:35:33,400 --> 00:35:34,800
If you want to hold a grudge,

425
00:35:36,240 --> 00:35:37,600
then do it on your own.

426
00:35:39,040 --> 00:35:41,720
If you cared about your son

427
00:35:42,560 --> 00:35:44,440
and saw what truly makes him happy,

428
00:35:46,360 --> 00:35:47,560
you wouldn’t be acting like this.

429
00:36:12,200 --> 00:36:13,760
Hey, hang on.

430
00:36:15,920 --> 00:36:16,640
Can you come with me?

431
00:36:18,880 --> 00:36:19,480
To where?

432
00:36:22,360 --> 00:36:23,080
Just trust me.

433
00:36:25,840 --> 00:36:26,400
Bay.

434
00:36:26,760 --> 00:36:27,680
If this doesn’t work,

435
00:36:28,520 --> 00:36:29,920
you won’t have to see me again.

436
00:37:13,720 --> 00:37:18,200
(Going back to my old school for a bit.
I’ll go straight home when I’m done.)

437
00:37:22,120 --> 00:37:24,960
-Why did you take me here?
-Come on, quick.

438
00:37:29,200 --> 00:37:29,760
You ready?

439
00:37:31,080 --> 00:37:32,160
Ready for what?

440
00:37:32,440 --> 00:37:34,000
I don’t even know why I’m here.

441
00:37:35,040 --> 00:37:36,040
You don’t have to know.

442
00:37:36,600 --> 00:37:38,160
Just do whatever you want to do.

443
00:37:38,520 --> 00:37:39,040
Okay?

444
00:37:40,320 --> 00:37:40,760
Let’s go.

445
00:37:46,320 --> 00:37:46,960
Come on.

446
00:37:47,360 --> 00:37:48,160
What is all this?

447
00:38:11,040 --> 00:38:12,040
It’s our prom.

448
00:38:15,320 --> 00:38:17,600
I didn’t want you to miss out on anything more.

449
00:38:19,240 --> 00:38:20,600
Isn’t this all we wanted, Sun?

450
00:38:25,520 --> 00:38:27,360
Just to live a normal life, like a normal kid.

451
00:38:30,080 --> 00:38:31,280
Make our own decisions.

452
00:38:36,040 --> 00:38:37,680
Do you think that’s impossible, Sun?

453
00:38:55,800 --> 00:38:56,640
I’m so sorry.

454
00:39:00,320 --> 00:39:02,800
-I should have kept fighting for us.
-It’s okay.

455
00:39:04,080 --> 00:39:04,760
It’s all right.

456
00:39:07,400 --> 00:39:08,320
I understand.

457
00:39:09,960 --> 00:39:11,160
And I’m not mad at you at all.

458
00:39:16,600 --> 00:39:19,400
Please be my genuine, simple Sun again.

459
00:39:37,880 --> 00:39:38,920
I’m really sorry.

460
00:39:40,760 --> 00:39:41,520
It’s okay.

461
00:39:42,680 --> 00:39:43,800
I know how you feel, really.

462
00:39:53,320 --> 00:39:56,040
♪ Ever since that day ♪

463
00:39:56,840 --> 00:40:02,240
♪ When you and I happened to meet, it’s like a dream ♪

464
00:40:02,600 --> 00:40:04,040
♪ ’Cause you’re the one ♪

465
00:40:04,040 --> 00:40:07,640
♪ Who came along and made my heart skip a beat ♪

466
00:40:07,920 --> 00:40:15,080
♪ It feels like I’ve finally found love ♪

467
00:40:57,280 --> 00:40:57,760
Pa!

468
00:41:12,920 --> 00:41:14,400
I’m the one who took Sun here.

469
00:41:23,280 --> 00:41:25,640
I’m sorry I didn’t ask you first.

470
00:41:27,040 --> 00:41:28,200
And I’m sorry

471
00:41:29,880 --> 00:41:31,240
that I didn’t tell you

472
00:41:32,440 --> 00:41:33,760
that I was dating Sun.

473
00:41:44,520 --> 00:41:45,880
But I really love him.

474
00:42:02,160 --> 00:42:02,960
I know

475
00:42:04,240 --> 00:42:06,000
you really hate my dad.

476
00:42:09,960 --> 00:42:11,640
But can you please not hate me?

477
00:42:18,160 --> 00:42:18,560
Pa.

478
00:42:22,120 --> 00:42:23,400
I’m begging you.

479
00:42:27,280 --> 00:42:30,720
Can you let me live like a normal kid for a night?

480
00:42:48,960 --> 00:42:50,600
Just don’t come home too late.

481
00:42:55,760 --> 00:42:57,560
Make sure you take him home by 11.

482
00:42:57,760 --> 00:42:58,400
You hear me?

483
00:43:00,200 --> 00:43:01,000
Yes, sir.

484
00:44:00,040 --> 00:44:03,240
Thank you for fighting for me.

485
00:44:04,080 --> 00:44:07,080
Thank you, too, for coming with me.

486
00:44:09,800 --> 00:44:12,080
Hey! What was that?!

487
00:44:12,520 --> 00:44:13,240
Do that again.

488
00:44:14,640 --> 00:44:16,240
I wasn’t ready for that.

489
00:44:17,640 --> 00:44:18,840
Please.

490
00:44:19,520 --> 00:44:20,480
Please pretty please.

491
00:44:21,000 --> 00:44:23,320
- Please pretty please.
-No, that’s enough.

492
00:44:23,320 --> 00:44:24,400
That’s enough.

493
00:44:24,760 --> 00:44:25,560
Why?

494
00:44:26,720 --> 00:44:28,040
We’ve got your dad’s approval.

495
00:44:37,920 --> 00:44:40,600
♪ You’re the only one I’ll ever give a Like ♪

496
00:44:40,720 --> 00:44:43,440
♪ Want, want you to come and be
a part of my life ♪

497
00:44:43,440 --> 00:44:46,320
♪ Morning, afternoon, or all night,
I’ll always make you smile ♪

498
00:44:46,320 --> 00:44:49,240
♪ No matter how many seconds pass,
I promise I’ll never make you cry ♪

499
00:44:49,240 --> 00:44:52,240
♪ I’ll hold you tight ♪

500
00:44:52,240 --> 00:44:55,680
♪ Never let you out of my sight ♪

501
00:44:55,960 --> 00:44:59,360
♪ Stay by my side ♪

502
00:44:59,360 --> 00:45:02,240
♪ We don’t need the stars to tell us this is real ♪

503
00:45:02,240 --> 00:45:06,120
♪ We don’t have to wait for some day
they say is special ♪

504
00:45:06,120 --> 00:45:10,320
♪ I’m giving you my whole heart ♪

505
00:45:12,480 --> 00:45:13,760
Where are you staying tonight, Bay?

506
00:45:14,000 --> 00:45:15,400
I can stay at my friend’s place, sir.

507
00:45:15,680 --> 00:45:18,280
It’s late. You can sleep with Sun tonight.

508
00:45:22,120 --> 00:45:25,200
If you walk away, don’t ever come back again, you brat!

509
00:45:25,760 --> 00:45:28,080
Unless you stop seeing that boy.

510
00:45:30,400 --> 00:45:32,360
You don’t have to carry this on
your shoulders, Bay.

511
00:45:37,760 --> 00:45:39,600
I’m here for you, always.
